.SS Abstract
This header provides CPU vendor/architecture detection and a runtime
version query function with a unified signature across supported CPUs.
.IP \(bu 2
At compile time, preprocessor checks detect the target CPU architecture
(Intel x86/x86\-64, AMD x86, ARM/AArch32/AArch64, PowerPC, RISC\-V,
etc.)
and define the corresponding \f[B]CPU_xxx\f[R] macro.
.IP \(bu 2
At runtime, \f[CR]CPU_VERSION\f[R] global variable gives you a static
C\-string containing the CPU vendor ID and a short
model/version/stepping description.
.IP \(bu 2
For x86\-family CPUs, CPUID is used to obtain vendor and version fields.
.IP \(bu 2
For ARM\-family CPUs, MIDR_EL1 or MIDR is read and parsed.
.IP \(bu 2
For other architectures, similar native registers or instructions can be
implemented in the same interface.
.PP
Purpose: Allows any codebase to get a consistent CPU identification
string without linking extra libraries, calling OS APIs, or using
sprintf/printf.
